Z||000029||qwikgta||05-10-2001||10:25 PM||||Lisa, as I was reading all the replys I was thinking of some ideas.  <P>1  Invert them in the hood, instead of out they would be in, like the hood of a 93+ Firebird.  Then they could vent the hot air out of the front<P>2. Use as side scoops, I think they are to long so cut them and mount them on both the rear 1/4 panel and the door.  When the door is closed it will flow air into the engine bay.  Like the side of the Testerrosa (sp).<P>3. As stated b4, try them on the trunk,  just to see if they look good there.  <P>BTW..where did you buy and how much, I have seen some like that in JC Whitney.  <P>Good luck<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000030||fiero56||05-10-2001||10:32 PM||||Lisa, <P>Put the left one on the right, and the right one on the left. So that they "meet" rather than face away from each other. Might look a little better.||||reg||1
