Z||000043||FieroLisa||05-11-2001||01:48 PM||||Steve-  the problem with making them fuctional is that if I cut a hole in my hood all that would do is get rain and weather in my front trunk area, unless I put them way towards the front of my car.<P>Fiero5- those don't look bad, but I'm not real big on those side scoops- only ones I like is the kit AusFiero made...<P>Well anyway I found someone who wants to buy them from me and try some experiments with them, which is what I would do if I had more time and a place to keep an extra hood! (Like trying to glass them in and seeing if that made them look more fluid and a part of the car)<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/daytona1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
